{"id": 83215, "acmi_id": "304419", "title": "Laurel Martyn", "title_annotation": "", "slug": "laurel-martyn", "creator_credit": "Peter Campbell and Australia Council", "credit_line": "", "headline_credit": "Australia, 1984", "record_type": "work", "type": "Film", "is_on_display": false, "last_on_display_place": null, "last_on_display_date": null, "is_context_indigenous": false, "material_description": "", "unpublished": false, "first_production_date": "1984-01-01T11:00:00+11:00", "brief_description": "<p>Episode of Series &#8220;Dance: Videos of Australian dancers and choreographers&#8221;.<br />\nLaurel Martyn trained in London with Phyllis Bedells and was awarded a choreographic scholarship under the auspices of Ninette de Valois. In this interview, Martyn recalls the highlights of her performing career with the &#8220;Sadler&#8217;s Wells Ballet&#8221; in England and the &#8220;Borovansky Ballet&#8221; in Australia and discusses her teaching method and philosophy. Through her company, &#8220;Ballet Vistoria&#8221;, Martyn encouraged the development of a distinctively Australian style of dance and introduced ballet to thousands of school children. Researched and interviewed by James Murdoch.</p>", "constellations_primary": [], "constellations_other": [], "recommendations": [], "title_for_label": "<p>Laurel Martyn</p>", "creator_credit_for_label": "<p>Peter Campbell and Australia Council</p>", "headline_credit_for_label": "<p>Australia, 1984</p>", "description": "<p>Episode of Series &#8220;Dance: Videos of Australian dancers and choreographers&#8221;.<br />\nLaurel Martyn trained in London with Phyllis Bedells and was awarded a choreographic scholarship under the auspices of Ninette de Valois. In this interview, Martyn recalls the highlights of her performing career with the &#8220;Sadler&#8217;s Wells Ballet&#8221; in England and the &#8220;Borovansky Ballet&#8221; in Australia and discusses her teaching method and philosophy. Through her company, &#8220;Ballet Vistoria&#8221;, Martyn encouraged the development of a distinctively Australian style of dance and introduced ballet to thousands of school children. Researched and interviewed by James Murdoch.</p>", "description_for_label": ["<p>Episode of Series &#8220;Dance: Videos of Australian dancers and choreographers&#8221;.<br />\nLaurel Martyn trained in London with Phyllis Bedells and was awarded a choreographic scholarship under the auspices of Ninette de Valois. In this interview, Martyn recalls the highlights of her performing career with the &#8220;Sadler&#8217;s Wells Ballet&#8221; in England and the &#8220;Borovansky Ballet&#8221; in Australia and discusses her teaching method and philosophy. Through her company, &#8220;Ballet Vistoria&#8221;, Martyn encouraged the development of a distinctively Australian style of dance and introduced ballet to thousands of school children. Researched and interviewed by James Murdoch.</p>"], "credit_line_for_label": "", "details": [{"label": "Duration", "display_values": ["01:01:00:00"]}, {"label": "Language", "display_values": ["English"]}, {"label": "Subject categories", "display_values": ["Archival, Cinemagazines & Newsreels", "Archival, Cinemagazines & Newsreels&nbsp;→ Archival materials", "Archival, Cinemagazines & Newsreels&nbsp;→ Interviews", "Documentary", "Documentary&nbsp;→ Documentary films - Australia", "Feature films", "Feature films&nbsp;→ Feature films - Australia", "Music & Performing Arts&nbsp;→ Ballet", "Music & Performing Arts&nbsp;→ Dancers", "Music & Performing Arts&nbsp;→ Dancers - Australia - Interviews", "People&nbsp;→ Martyn, Laurel"]}, {"label": "Sound/audio", "display_values": ["Sound"]}, {"label": "Colour", "display_values": ["Colour"]}], "stats": {"tap_count": 0}, "links": [], "creators_primary": [{"id": 1535300, "name": "Peter Campbell", "creator_id": 21521, "creator_wikidata_id": null, "role": "producer", "role_id": 960, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 1535299, "name": "Australia Council", "creator_id": 